  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "header"
   },
   "source": [
    "# 🌊 Surf AI Agent - Google Colab Demo\n",
    "\n",
    "**Computer Use AI - Control GUI with Natural Language**\n",
    "\n",
    "A flexible AI agent that converts natural language to GUI actions (click, type, scroll, etc.). Works with ANY LLM provider!\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## ✨ Features\n",
    "\n",
    "- ✅ **Multi-Provider**: OpenAI, Mistral, Anthropic, Groq, Ollama, etc.\n",
    "- ✅ **9 Action Types**: click, double_click, scroll, type, press_key, move_mouse, wait, focus, screenshot\n",
    "- ✅ **Natural Language**: "Click at 100,200 and type Hello" → generates actions\n",
    "- ✅ **Configurable**: Set any base URL and API key\n",
    "- ✅ **Lightweight**: Runs in Colab with minimal resources\n",
    "- ✅ **Open Source**: MIT License\n",
    "\n",
    "## 🚀 Quick Start\n",
    "\n",
    "Run all cells in order, or jump to specific sections below."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "install"
   },
   "source": [
    "# Install Surf AI Agent\n",
    "!git clone https://github.com/madgeret-del/surf.git\n",
    "%cd surf\n",
    "!pip install -r requirements.txt\n",
    "\n",
    "print('✅ Surf AI Agent installed successfully!')"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "config-section"
   },
   "source": [
    "## ⚙️ Configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "Set up your LLM provider. Surf works with ANY provider that has an OpenAI-compatible API."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "config-setup"
   },
   "source": [
    "from surf import SurfConfig\n",
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set your configuration\n",
    "# You can use environment variables or set directly\n",
    "\n",
    "# Option 1: Set directly (replace with your values)\n",
    "config = SurfConfig(\n",
    "    base_url='https://api.openai.com/v1',  # Change to your provider\n",
    "    api_key='',  # Set your API key here or use env var\n",
    "    model='gpt-4o-mini',  # Model to use\n",
    "    temperature=0.7,  # Creativity (0.0-2.0)\n",
    "    max_tokens=4096,  # Max tokens in response\n",
    "    verbose=True  # Show detailed output\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Option 2: Use environment variables (recommended for Colab)\n",
    "# Set these in Colab secrets or use os.environ\n",
    "# os.environ['SURF_API_KEY'] = 'your-api-key'\n",
    "# os.environ['SURF_BASE_URL'] = 'https://api.openai.com/v1'\n",
    "# config = SurfConfig.from_env()\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Configuration ready!')\n",
    "print(f'Base URL: {config.base_url}')\n",
    "print(f'Model: {config.model}')"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "set-api-key"
   },
   "source": [
    "# @title Set API Key\n",
    "# @markdown Enter your API key below\n",
    "\n",
    "# Use this for easy API key input in Colab\n",
    "from google.colab import userdata\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    # Try to get from Colab secrets\n",
    "    api_key = userdata.get('SURF_API_KEY')\n",
    "    print('✅ API key loaded from Colab secrets')\n",
    "except:\n",
    "    # Fallback to manual input\n",
    "    api_key = input('Enter your API key: ')\n",
    "    print('✅ API key set')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Update config with API key\n",
    "config.api_key = api_key\n",
    "print('API key configured!')"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "quick-test"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 🧪 Quick Test\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's test Surf with a simple command."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "first-test"
   },
   "source": [
    "from surf import SurfAgent\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create agent\n",
    "agent = SurfAgent(config)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test with a simple instruction\n",
    "result = agent.run('Click at coordinates 100, 200 and type Hello World')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Display results\n",
    "print(f'✅ Success: {result.success}')\n",
    "print(f'📝 Message: {result.message}')\n",
    "print(f'⚡ Actions executed: {len(result.actions_executed)}')\n",
    "\n",
    "for i, action in enumerate(result.actions_executed, 1):\n",
    "    print(f'  {i}. {action.action_type}: {action.params}')"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "provider-presets"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 🎯 Provider Presets\n",
    "\n",
    "Quick configuration for popular providers:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "presets-code"
   },
   "source": [
    "# Provider presets\n",
    "providers = {\n",
    "    'openai': {\n",
    "        'base_url': 'https://api.openai.com/v1',\n",
    "        'models': ['gpt-4o-mini', 'gpt-4', 'gpt-3.5-turbo'],\n",
    "        'api_key_env': 'OPENAI_API_KEY'\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    'mistral': {\n",
    "        'base_url': 'https://api.mistral.ai/v1',\n",
    "        'models': ['mistral-large', 'mistral-small', 'mixtral-8x7b'],\n",
    "        'api_key_env': 'MISTRAL_API_KEY'\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    'anthropic': {\n",
    "        'base_url': 'https://api.anthropic.com/v1',\n",
    "        'models': ['claude-3-haiku', 'claude-3-sonnet', 'claude-3-opus'],\n",
    "        'api_key_env': 'ANTHROPIC_API_KEY'\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    'groq': {\n",
    "        'base_url': 'https://api.groq.com/v1',\n",
    "        'models': ['llama3-8b', 'llama3-70b', 'mixtral-8x7b'],\n",
    "        'api_key_env': 'GROQ_API_KEY'\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    'ollama': {\n",
    "        'base_url': 'http://localhost:11434/v1',\n",
    "        'models': ['llama3.2', 'mistral', 'phi3'],\n",
    "        'api_key_env': None  # Usually not needed for local\n",
    "    }\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Switch to a provider\n",
    "def use_provider(provider_name, model=None):\n",
    "    provider = providers.get(provider_name)\n",
    "    if not provider:\n",
    "        print(f'Unknown provider: {provider_name}')\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "    \n",
    "    config = SurfConfig(\n",
    "        base_url=provider['base_url'],\n",
    "        model=model or provider['models'][0],\n",
    "        verbose=True\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Try to get API key from environment\n",
    "    if provider['api_key_env']:\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            from google.colab import userdata\n",
    "            config.api_key = userdata.get(provider['api_key_env'])\n",
    "        except:\n",
    "            pass\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return config\n",
    "\n",
    "# Example usage:\n",
    "# config = use_provider('mistral')\n",
    "# agent = SurfAgent(config)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Available providers:', list(providers.keys()))"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "action-examples"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 🎮 Action Examples\n",
    "\n",
    "Try these example commands with Surf:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "examples-code"
   },
   "source": [
    "# Example commands\n",
    "examples = [\n",
    "    'Click at coordinates 100, 200 and type Hello World',\n",
    "    'Move the mouse to 500, 300 and double-click',\n",
    "    'Scroll down by 100 pixels',\n",
    "    'Press Ctrl+S to save the document',\n",
    "    'Wait 2 seconds, then click at 200, 200',\n",
    "    'Type my name and press Enter',\n",
    "    'Move mouse to 100, 100, click, then move to 300, 300',\n",
    "    'Scroll up by 50 pixels',\n",
    "    'Double-click at the center of the screen',\n",
    "    'Press Alt+Tab to switch windows'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test all examples\n",
    "agent = SurfAgent(config)\n",
    "\n",
    "for example in examples[:3]:  # Test first 3 to save API calls\n",
    "    print(f'\\n🎯 Testing: {example}')\n",
    "    result = agent.run(example)\n",
    "    print(f'   Actions: {len(result.actions_executed)}')\n",
    "    for action in result.actions_executed:\n",
    "        print(f'   - {action.action_type}: {action.params}')"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "programmatic-actions"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 💻 Programmatic Actions\n",
    "\n",
    "Create and execute actions directly without using the LLM."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "programmatic-code"
   },
   "source": [
    "from surf.actions import (\n",
    "    ClickAction, DoubleClickAction, TypeAction, PressKeyAction,\n",
    "    ScrollAction, MoveMouseAction, WaitAction, FocusAction\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create a sequence of actions programmatically\n",
    "actions = [\n",
    "    ClickAction(x=100, y=200, button='left'),\n",
    "    TypeAction(text='Hello from programmatic actions!'),\n",
    "    PressKeyAction(key='Enter'),\n",
    "    WaitAction(seconds=1.0),\n",
    "    MoveMouseAction(x=300, y=400),\n",
    "    DoubleClickAction(x=300, y=400),\n",
    "    ScrollAction(delta_x=0, delta_y=100),\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Execute the actions\n",
    "result = agent.run_actions(actions)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'✅ Executed {len(result.actions_executed)} actions')\n",
    "print(f'❌ Failed: {len(result.actions_failed)} actions')\n",
    "\n",
    "for action in result.actions_executed:\n",
    "    print(f'  ✓ {action}')"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "e2b-integration"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 🖥️ E2B Integration (Real GUI Control)\n",
    "\n",
    "To connect to a **real desktop environment** like E2B, set a custom action executor."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "e2b-code"
   },
   "source": [
    """\n",
    "# E2B Integration Example\n",
    "\n",
    "# First, install E2B client:\n",
    "# !pip install e2b\n",
    "\n",
    "from surf import SurfAgent, SurfConfig, ActionResult\n",
    "from surf.actions import BaseAction\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define E2B executor\n",
    "class E2BExecutor:\n",
    "    def __init__(self):\n",
    "        # Initialize E2B client\n",
    "        # from e2b import Session\n",
    "        # self.session = Session()\n",
    "        pass\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def execute(self, action: BaseAction) -> ActionResult:\n",
    "        # Convert Surf action to E2B action\n",
    "        action_type = action.action_type\n",
    "        params = action.params\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Example mappings:\n",
    "        if action_type == 'click':\n",
    "            # session.click(x=params['x'], y=params['y'])\n",
    "            print(f'Would click at ({params[\"x\"]}, {params[\"y\"]})')\n",
    "            return ActionResult(success=True, message='Click sent to E2B')\n",
    "        \n",
    "        elif action_type == 'type':\n",
    "            # session.type_text(params['text'])\n",
    "            print(f'Would type: {params[\"text\"]}')\n",
    "            return ActionResult(success=True, message='Type sent to E2B')\n",
    "        \n",
    "        elif action_type == 'scroll':\n",
    "            # session.scroll(delta_x=params['delta_x'], delta_y=params['delta_y'])\n",
    "            print(f'Would scroll by ({params[\"delta_x\"]}, {params[\"delta_y\"]})')\n",
    "            return ActionResult(success=True, message='Scroll sent to E2B')\n",
    "        \n",
    "        elif action_type == 'press_key':\n",
    "            # session.press_key(params['key'])\n",
    "            print(f'Would press key: {params[\"key\"]}')\n",
    "            return ActionResult(success=True, message='Key press sent to E2B')\n",
    "        \n",
    "        elif action_type == 'move_mouse':\n",
    "            # session.move_mouse(x=params['x'], y=params['y'])\n",
    "            print(f'Would move mouse to ({params[\"x\"]}, {params[\"y\"]})')\n",
    "            return ActionResult(success=True, message='Mouse move sent to E2B')\n",
    "        \n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            return ActionResult(success=False, message=f'Action {action_type} not supported')\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def __call__(self, action: BaseAction) -> ActionResult:\n",
    "        return self.execute(action)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Usage:\n",
    "# executor = E2BExecutor()\n",
    "# agent = SurfAgent(config)\n",
    "# agent.set_action_executor(executor)\n",
    "# result = agent.run('Click on the start menu')\n",
    "\n",
    "print('E2B integration example loaded!')\n",
    "print('Uncomment and install e2b to use real GUI control')"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "web-interface"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 🌐 Web Interface in Colab\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the Surf web server directly in Colab and access it via ngrok tunnel."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "web-code"
   },
   "source": [
    "# Run web server in Colab\n",
    "!pip install pyngrok flask\n",
    "\n",
    "from surf.web.server import app\n",
    "from pyngrok import ngrok\n",
    "import threading\n",
    "import time\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set your config for the web server\n",
    "import os\n",
    "os.environ['SURF_API_KEY'] = api_key  # Use the API key from earlier\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run Flask in background\n",
    "def run_flask():\n",
    "    app.run(host='0.0.0.0', port=5000, debug=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "thread = threading.Thread(target=run_flask, daemon=True)\n",
    "thread.start()\n",
    "time.sleep(2)  # Wait for server to start\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create ngrok tunnel\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    public_url = ngrok.connect(5000).public_url\n",
    "    print(f'✅ Web interface live at: {public_url}')\n",
    "    print('📝 Note: This URL will expire when you disconnect from Colab')\n",
    "    print('⏰ Keep this cell running to keep the server alive')\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print(f'❌ Error creating tunnel: {e}')\n",
    "    print('Make sure ngrok is authenticated: !ngrok authtoken YOUR_TOKEN')\n",
    "    print('Get token from: https://dashboard.ngrok.com/get-started/your-authtoken')"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
